se the U.S has to support Ukraine  because it has the sophisticated  military  um weapons that Ukraine needs but um he  wants Europe to do more  okay  um the midterms of course are being  closely watched around the world not  least in Moscow and Beijing do these  elections have the potential to shape  U.S foreign policy towards Russia and  China  um most certainly I think that  um you know I think if the Republicans  take the house which is usually normal  in a midterm election that the Congress  switches to a different party than the  party that's in the white house then of  course it'll be a raucous two years of  Investigations into Hunter Biden the  Afghanistan withdrawal and perhaps even  articles of impeachment and countries  like Russia and China that are using  disinformation to sow Discord within the  United States will certainly use this as  an opportunity to divide Americans even  more in a very Polo polarized atmosphere  in the run-up to 2024 and the world is  watching um the state of democracy in  the United States right now  so the state of democracy is at stake as  it were what about EU U.S relations will  transatlantic relations and this is your  bread and butter well transatlantic  relations be affected if for example the  House and Senate flip and Biden becomes  a lame duck  um as I mentioned  overwhelming the partisan support for  Ukraine and also also for NATO NATO NATO  is very popular Institution for  Democrats and Republicans alike and I  think there was incredible cohesion  between the United States and Europe  with Russia's war against Ukraine and I  I don't see that faltering immediately  but there is of course friction on the  horizon specifically with you know  Germany and Europe's relations with  China there's also growing Hardline  um uh you know  cooperation between Democrats and  Republicans on the U.S stance toward  China and  um also that the Europeans also need to  do more in their own backyard and that  military spending is necessary so I  think that there's frictions there and  also with Biden's inflation reduction  act there have also been of course  disadvantages for Europe because uh by  this policy of promoting the middle  class is going to hurt European  companies involved in the electric  vehicle industry  so to thank you very much that was  suited David wilp director of the Berlin  office of the German Marshall fund  good to see you

